# A Final Attack behind the Marksman's own shots, and the reason a Final
# Attack can state a reach at all: GMS gives the split its own mobCount and its
# own hitbox, so behind Snipe -- a swing that reaches one -- it still reaches
# ten. A Final Attack otherwise falls on the one enemy its swing picked, which
# is what final_attack_max_enemies reads as 1.
#
# Which swings it follows is the group rather than a list of names: GMS names
# Piercing Arrow, Snipe and the cartridge, and those three carry the tag. High
# Speed Shot, Perfect Shot and Surge Bolt are deliberately not among them.
#
# GMS's readout says "Landing a hit with Full Burst Shot after using ..." and
# then names the cartridge among the skills it follows, which makes the
# sentence name that skill as an alternative to itself. Grandis Library states
# it plainly -- successful attacks from those skills release the burst -- and
# Final Aim's own text ("triggered up to 13 times") only makes sense if the
# default is once per cast. Once per cast is what this is.
name: "Split Shot"
description:
  "Magically enchants your arrows to explode as they approach the enemy, "
  "releasing countless more arrows."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_MARKSMAN_V skill_order: 2 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 120.0
follows_skill_tag: SKILL_TAG_MARKSMANSHIP
final_attack_max_enemies: 10
buff {
  duration_seconds: 72.0
  base {
    final_attack_chance: 1.0
    final_attack_pct: 6.06
    final_attack_lines: 5
    ied_pct: 0.25
  }
  per_level { final_attack_pct: 0.24 }
}
